
  LazyAF debug sidecar - the pipeline is PAUSED at a breakpoint.

  /workspace          the paused run's workspace volume (READ-WRITE)
  /workspace/repo     the checked-out repo at the commit under debug
  /workspace/home     the persisted HOME shared across the run's steps
  /workspace/.control step config drop-box (written per step by the backend)

  EDITS UNDER /workspace ARE SEEN BY THE RESUMED STEP.
  This container shares the volume with the step that is about to run - it is
  not a copy and there is no undo. That is the point of a debug re-run, and
  it is also the way to break one.

  You are uid 1000 (lazyaf), the same user the step runs as, so nothing you
  create here is ownership-poisoned for the step. `sudo` is available.

  The step has NOT started: no step container exists yet. This shell is a
  sidecar on the workspace, not a shell inside the step.

  Controls (also available as plain `lazyaf debug ...` subcommands):
    Ctrl-]      drop to the debug> prompt
    @resume     continue to the next breakpoint
    @abort      end the session and cancel the run
    @status     session state, breakpoints hit/pending, time left
    @help       this list

  The session ends on its own when the timer expires - `@status` shows how
  much is left and `lazyaf debug extend` buys more.

